Extra PHP versions (8.2 - 8.4) for Sentora on Ubuntu 26.04
==========================================================

The installer downloads sentora-php-<version>-ubuntu26.04-amd64.tar.gz from the
GitHub release of RusTus/sentora-installers-2027 and installs each in /opt/sentora-php/<version>/ as the service
sentora-php<version>-fpm. These builds are not updated by apt: when PHP
publishes a release for one of them (https://www.php.net/releases/), rebuild
and update it with the two scripts here.

1. Build (as root on an Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 machine, ideally a spare VM, since
   it installs compilers and -dev packages):

       bash build-sentora-php.sh 8.3.37

   It downloads php-8.3.37.tar.xz from php.net, checks its SHA-256 against
   php.net, builds it with the same options as the shipped bundles, checks it
   runs, and writes sentora-php-8.3-ubuntu26.04-amd64.tar.gz in the current
   folder. Compiling takes 10-30 minutes depending on the machine.

2. Publish: attach the .tar.gz to the "current" sentora-installers-2027 release on
   GitHub, replacing the old file (new installs and step 3 use it).

3. Update a running server (as root on that server):

       bash update-sentora-php.sh 8.3

   It downloads the bundle from the "current" GitHub release (TAG=<tag> picks
   another), checks its SHA-256 against the release, checks the new build runs with the
   server's current settings, swaps the program files (keeping etc/: php.ini,
   php-fpm.conf, the pool), restarts sentora-php8.3-fpm, and puts the old
   files back if it does not start. Domains on that version are only offline
   for the few seconds of the restart.

Security support (PHP project):
   8.1  ended 31 Dec 2025 - no more releases, nothing to rebuild
   8.2  until 31 Dec 2026
   8.3  until 31 Dec 2027
   8.4  until 31 Dec 2028

PHP 7.1 - only for moving old Sentora 2.0.2 websites
====================================================

PHP 7.1 has had no security fixes since 1 Dec 2019. It is offered only so that websites
moved from an old Sentora 2.0.2 server that do not run on PHP 8 yet keep working while
they are fixed. The installer installs it switched OFF and does not start it; an
administrator switches it on in PHP Versions for a move (the page asks first), and should
move each site to PHP 8 and switch 7.1 off again.

Build (as root, on Ubuntu 24.04 or 26.04 amd64):

       bash build-sentora-php71.sh

It builds PHP 7.1.33 (the last 7.1 release) with its own OpenSSL 1.1.1w, curl 7.88.1,
libxml2 2.9.14 and libmcrypt 2.5.8 compiled in (PHP 7.1 does not build against Ubuntu
26.04's OpenSSL 3 or libxml2), checks every source against its published checksum, and
writes sentora-php-7.1-ubuntu26.04-amd64.tar.gz. Attach it to the "current" release like
the other bundles. Besides the C library it links only zlib, libpng16, libjpeg-turbo,
freetype, libwebp and gmp, which are the same on Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04. No intl.

Add it to a server installed before it (as root):

       sentora-php-install 7.1
